      "CVE": "CVE-2026-96636",
      "Description": "Pillow is a Python imaging library. Prior to 13.0.0, MpoImageFile.seek() and DcxImageFile.seek() reparse later MPO or DCX frames and replace self._size without rerunning Image._decompression_bomb_check(). A crafted multi-frame image can use a tiny first frame to pass Image.open() and then declare an over-limit later frame. Normal frame iteration through seek(), load(), or ImageSequence.Iterator can decode that frame and commit hundreds of megabytes or more, causing memory-exhaustion denial of service. This issue is fixed in version 13.0.0.",
      "Threats": [
        {
          "Type": "Impact",
          "Severity": "moderate"
        }
      ],
      "References": [
        {
          "URL": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-96636.html",
          "Description": "CVE-2026-96636"
        },
        {
          "URL": "https://bugzilla.suse.com/1286802",
          "Description": "SUSE Bug 1286802"
        }
      ],
